 "text": "Hey, good to have you here. How are you? Put it in the refrigerator the night before, and get it out just after waking up on Saturday. Keep it between the Coldest spot and fridge calendar. Blocks are much more effective, they don't thaw nearby fridges, and they fit easily in the coldest spot. Keep it well wrapped and never overcrowd the fridge. If you leave it in at weekend, it can easily ice up. Tell him to leave it until Saturday, and only look inside if the cold spot has gone cold. Yes, pour it down the sink while filling it with fresh cold water. Melted water can leave a puddle that can spoil the fridge.",
